        "hypothesis": "One statically scheduled OpenMP team processing independent column pipelines should accelerate substantial workloads on four ARM64 cores while preserving each column's arithmetic order.",
        "id": "fd34e6dc39ac40ec",
        "ordinal": 1,
        "parent_id": null,
        "role": "C",
        "source_commits": [],
        "sources": [],
        "transformations": {
          "files": [
            "src/est_matriz_seq.c"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Fuse the existing eight stages into complete per-column pipelines, retaining means before sorting and variance after sorting.",
            "Use one static OpenMP parallel-for when multiple columns provide at least 262144 estimated C*R^2 work units; keep smaller workloads serial.",
            "Zero-initialize private mode scratch for deterministic concurrent and repeated calls. Preserve bubble sort, counting loops, float mode selection, column-major storage, and formatted I/O."
          ]
        },
